-- title:
--   Logarithmic growth rate of the rounded band numerator
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)=\operatorname{typedOutputs}(n)$ be the positive output-table count from the executable block schedule, and let $B(n)=\lceil\sqrt{T(n)}\rceil$ be its integer square-root ceiling, the defined band numerator. Write $E=128H_2(1/256)$, where $H_2$ is binary entropy in bits. Then
--
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log B(n)}{\log n}=\frac E5.
--   $$
--
--   This assigns an exact exponent to the rounded numerator used to compute the band size, with the integer rounding included in the statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/BandScales.lean#L75-L102

